 they obscure is emptiness  over the course of the saw series we get  multiple looks at the actual  face of jigsaw killer john kramer but we  also see him in a pig mask  which is first introduced in the 2004  original  as a detail that one of his victims  recalls later in the series the mask is  revealed to be a tribute to the year of  the pig  during which jigsaw began his work in  chinese zodiac legend  the pig can symbolize laziness the  antithesis of the will to live that john  attempts to divine in each of his test  subjects  the pig is also the final animal of the  zodiac cycle which can be read as a  symbol of john's cancer diagnosis  with his serial killing being the final  chapter of his life  a pig mask containing a chloroform rag  was the first tool that john  ever used to subdue a test subject he  chose it personally as a representation  of his pessimistic worldview  and the slow decay of his body from  cancer however the pig  also represents rebirth which does  require a death  so while it may appear paradoxical at  first it actually makes sense to read  the pig  as a symbol of both beginning and ending  this squares up with jigsaw's motivation  and tactics despite the frequent deaths  of his subjects  he genuinely does want to give them a  second chance at life  the cast of the killers in 2011's you're  next  are credited by both the names of the  human characters they play  as well as the name of the animal masks  they wear the crew includes a lamb  a tiger and a fox behind the mask though  lamb and tiger are brothers and  represent just about the only instance  of familial loyalty in the film  two other brothers felix and crispin  turn out to be in on a plot to massacre  their own family  in order to collect an inheritance  animal masks  are the perfect representation of a home  invasion in which some wild and  destructive force from the outside  threatens the balance within the home  you might expect a wolf to be among this  invasive animal cohort  